81:eg-binpress-2016	https://erangalperin.com/2016/02/11/startup-postmortem-binpress/	Eran Galperin — "Startup Postmortem: Binpress", published 2016-02-11 (schema dateModified 2023-09-15; this task did not diff the live page against a Wayback capture of the original 2016 version within its time box, so treat the modification date as an open, named caveat rather than a confirmed content edit), consulted 2026-08-06. Founder's own retrospective account of Binpress (2010-2016), a marketplace for developer code libraries and later digital products, co-founded with Adam: growth from roughly 10 users in the first two months to a $30k/month sales peak; a February 2013 acceptance into the 500 Startups accelerator on the strength of a $20k-in-one-month local maximum; a seed round of almost $1M raised during the accelerator; a September 2014 pivot decision after roughly a year of stalled growth against half the raised money already spent; a January 2015 relaunch that also failed to grow; and the founders' explicit decision, in Galperin's words, that "it was time to move on" — shopping the whole company for sale, failing to close that sale, and settling for selling the assets only (site and code-base) while dissolving the company and returning what they could to investors. Founder's own account: weaker evidence class per §5, attributed as such in the prose.
82:kvk-eenmanszaak-2026	https://www.kvk.nl/stoppen-en-uitschrijven/eenmanszaak-uitschrijven/	KVK (Dutch Chamber of Commerce) — "Eenmanszaak uitschrijven", consulted 2026-08-06. Official guidance on deregistering a sole proprietorship from the Handelsregister: the deregistration is done online via Mijn KVK with DigiD, is free, and is definitive; the owner must keep filing tax returns until the Belastingdienst confirms otherwise; and KVK itself forwards the deregistration to the Belastingdienst rather than the owner having to notify them separately. The eenmanszaak side of the winding-up fork (§5b's "how to wind up cleanly" chapter-28 subject).
83:kvk-turboliquidatie-2026	https://www.kvk.nl/stoppen-en-uitschrijven/een-rechtspersoon-beeindigen-via-de-turboliquidatie/	KVK — "Een rechtspersoon beëindigen via de turboliquidatie", "Bijgewerkt" (updated) 2026-08-04, consulted 2026-08-06. Official guidance on the fast-track dissolution route for a bv (and other legal persons): usable only when there are no baten (assets) left at the moment of dissolution, with an explicit warning that the definition of baten is broader than owners expect; since the tijdelijke wet Transparantie turboliquidatie (15 November 2023), the board must file financial accounting documents with KVK within fourteen days of the dissolution resolution, and can face personal liability or a bestuursverbod (director's disqualification) for misuse. The bv side of the winding-up fork, and the source for why "just stop" is not in fact simple for an incorporated business.
